  "client_brief": "We are preparing a worked lesson excerpt from Meridian Academy's Operations Analytics programme. Choose a complete teaching unit: the learner should see the setup, follow the example and reach the conclusion. Removing pauses is useful only if it does not remove the thinking time needed to understand the screen. The spoken explanation, board or interface and captions must agree. Deliver a proper lesson video and its cover. The release pack must contain a complete authorised explanation; a silent five-second visual cannot stand in for a lesson.\n\nThe commission\n\n Worked lesson excerpt: 1 named export. The worked example reaches its stated conclusion. The board or screen text is readable. The captions follow the spoken explanation.\n\n Lesson cover: 1 named export. The lesson number is correct. The topic is readable.\n\nUse the supplied approved copy and factual records. Permission restrictions in the owner's notes take precedence over inclusion in a source table.\n- Video delivery means a playable MP4, not a storyboard, still montage PDF or editing log. Audio expectations are stated on each film. Speech-led work requires supplied or explicitly authorised synthetic speech; do not invent documentary speech.\n- Authored animation can exceed the duration of still source images. Live-action edits require adequate distinct footage; looping a short clip is not a substitute for the missing coverage.\n\nUse the attached brand identity and the source files listed in the asset manifest. The output register defines exact filenames, pages, sizes and record bindings. Supporting previews are welcome but cannot replace those files.",
  "brand_identity": {
    "brand_name": "Meridian Academy",
    "tagline": "Practical skills for people who already have a job.",
    "sector": "Professional education (self-paced online academy)",
    "founded_place_size": "Founded 2021 in Portland, Oregon. A four person team running one course.",
    "about": "Meridian Academy sells a single self-paced program, Operations Analytics for Working Managers, at two hundred and ninety dollars. Our learners are thirty to fifty, mid-career, watching lessons late at night after their own workday. We are not a bootcamp and we are not a university. We teach one useful thing well and we respect the viewer's time and intelligence.",
    "personality": [
      "Plain",
      "Adult",
      "Calm",
      "Credible",
      "Unhurried"
    ],
    "audience": "Working managers aged thirty to fifty, paying with their own money, fitting the course around a full-time job. They want a working skill, not a transformation story, and they distrust anything that feels like marketing.",
    "price_positioning": "Mid-market. A two hundred and ninety dollar considered purchase. The register sits between an impulse-priced tutorial and a formal institution: competent, quiet, self-funded professional development.",
    "palette": [
      {
        "name": "Deep Slate",
        "hex": "#2E3A45"
      },
      {
        "name": "Cream Stock",
        "hex": "#F4EFE4"
